R.note:
For your name’s sake, Lord, preserve my life;
    in your righteousness, bring me out of trouble.
1

U.note:
Then I will teach transgressors your ways,
    so that sinners will turn back to you. | Cleanse me with hyssop, and I will be clean; wash me, and I will be whiter than snow.
8 Let me hear joy and gladness;

may sinners vanish from the earth, and the wicked be no more. | He makes winds his messengers,[a]
    flames of fire his servants. / I will sing to the Lord all my life;
    I will sing praise to my God as long as I live.
